---
import ResourceLayout from '../../components/ResourceLayout.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import InfographicViewer from '../../components/InfographicViewer.astro';
import ExternalResource from '../../components/ExternalResource.astro';
---

<ResourceLayout
  icon="🩺"
  eyebrow="Healthcare navigation"
  title="Finding Healthcare"
  introduction="Learn where to go when you need healthcare in British Columbia, including family doctors, walk-in clinics, urgent care, virtual care, and emergency services."
>
  <VideoEmbed
    title="Finding Healthcare in British Columbia"
    videoId="_xln4IlNejY"
    description="Watch this short video to learn how to access healthcare services, find a healthcare provider, and choose the right place to receive care."
  />

  <InfographicViewer
    title="Where to Go for Care"
    description="Learn where to seek medical care depending on your symptoms, including family doctors, walk-in clinics, urgent care centres, and emergency departments."
    previewSrc="/infographics/mental-health/where-to-go-for-care-en.png"
    previewAlt="Preview of the Where to Go for Care infographic"
    languages={[
      {
        label: 'English',
        href: '/infographics/mental-health/where-to-go-for-care-en.png',
        lang: 'en',
      },
      {
        label: 'ਪੰਜਾਬੀ',
        href: '/infographics/mental-health/where-to-go-for-care-pa.png',
        lang: 'pa',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <ExternalResource
  icon="🇨🇦"
  source="WelcomeBC"
  title="Newcomers' Guide to British Columbia"
  description="Multilingual information about healthcare, MSP, finding a family doctor, emergency care, and other essential newcomer services."
  href="https://www.welcomebc.ca/"
/>

<ExternalResource
  icon="🏛️"
  source="Government of British Columbia"
  title="Health Care in British Columbia"
  description="Official information about Medical Services Plan (MSP), finding healthcare providers, immunizations, and health services."
  href="https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/health"
 />

<ExternalResource
  icon="☎️"
  source="HealthLink BC"
  title="HealthLink BC (8-1-1)"
  description="Speak with a registered nurse, pharmacist, dietitian, or health service navigator 24/7. Interpretation is available in over 130 languages."
  href="https://www.healthlinkbc.ca/"
/>

<ExternalResource
  icon="🏥"
  source="Fraser Health"
  title="South Asian & Newcomer Resources"
  description="Find multilingual healthcare navigation guides, primary care directories, interpreter information, and newcomer health resources."
  href="https://www.fraserhealth.ca/"
/>
  <section>
    <h2>Family doctors and nurse practitioners</h2>
    <p>
      A family doctor or nurse practitioner is usually your first point of
      contact for non-emergency healthcare. They provide routine checkups,
      manage chronic conditions, order tests, prescribe medications, and refer
      patients to specialists when needed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Walk-in clinics and Urgent & Primary Care Centres</h2>
    <p>
      If you do not have a regular healthcare provider or need care the same
      day for a non-life-threatening problem, a walk-in clinic or Urgent &
      Primary Care Centre (UPCC) may be appropriate. They treat illnesses and
      injuries that cannot wait for a routine appointment but are not medical
      emergencies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Virtual care</h2>
    <p>
      Some medical concerns can be assessed by telephone or video appointment.
      Virtual care is convenient for many health concerns but may not be
      suitable if a physical examination or emergency treatment is required.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>HealthLink BC (8-1-1)</h2>
    <p>
      HealthLink BC is available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. By calling
      8-1-1, you can speak with a registered nurse, pharmacist, dietitian, or
      health service navigator. Interpretation is available in more than 130
      languages to help you receive information in your preferred language.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Community organizations</h2>
    <p>
      Settlement organizations such as ISSofBC, MOSAIC, and S.U.C.C.E.S.S.
      can help newcomers understand the healthcare system, register for MSP,
      connect with healthcare providers, and access interpreter services and
      other community supports.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="notice">
    <strong>Know when to call 911.</strong>
    <p>
      Call 911 immediately if someone has severe chest pain, difficulty
      breathing, signs of stroke, major bleeding, loss of consciousness, or any
      other life-threatening emergency.
    </p>
  </aside>
</ResourceLayout>